@* shadcn's natural-language picker parses "next tuesday" in the browser. Parsing a date is the
   server's job here: it already has to, because a client-side parse is a convenience and the
   value still arrives as text. up-validate echoes back what it understood, so the reader sees the
   interpretation before submitting rather than after. *@
<form method="post" action="/reminders" up-target=".preview" class="w-[420px]">
    <AntiforgeryToken />
    <Field>
        <FieldLabel For="dpn-when">When</FieldLabel>
        <Input id="dpn-when" name="when" value="next tuesday at 9" up-validate
               autocomplete="off" />
        <FieldDescription>Understood as <b>Tuesday 17 March, 09:00</b>.</FieldDescription>
    </Field>
</form>
